/-!
# Inner/outer residual comparison for reverse Δ₀

The central-quotient transports retain the covering kernels and relative
normality. The M₁₁ and Suzuki alternatives are excluded by their actual
automorphism theorems. Given an M₁₂ component quotient and the genuine
16.1.5(4) table, the comparison constructs both A₅ residual equivalences.

The Lie-family and remaining odd/sporadic exclusions are still required
before the unconditional component identification can be assembled here.
No table-comparison conclusion is assumed as an earlier source input.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
proof of 16.4.11(2), printed p.1193, comparing 16.1.4–5.
-/
